"""The atlas page uses the existing archive shell and self-hosted map data."""
import html
import json
from pathlib import Path


def render_atlas():
    h = html.escape
    data = json.loads((Path(__file__).parent / 'archive/maps/assyria-atlas.json').read_text())
    snapshots = data['snapshots']
    options = ''.join(f'<option value="{i}" {"selected" if i == 4 else ""}>{abs(s["year"])} BCE - {h(s["title"])}</option>' for i, s in enumerate(snapshots))
    sources = ''.join(f'<li id="atlas-source-{h(s["id"])}"><a href="{h(s["url"])}" target="_blank" rel="noopener">{h(s["title"])}</a><p>{h(s["author"])}. {h(s["note"])}</p></li>' for s in data['sources'])
    chronology = ''.join(f'<li><strong>{abs(s["year"])} BCE - {h(s["title"])}</strong><p>{h(s["summary"])}</p><p class="muted">{h(s["caution"])}</p></li>' for s in snapshots)
    return f'''<main id="main" class="wrap section atlas-page">
<div class="page-heading atlas-heading"><span class="eyebrow">THE HISTORICAL ATLAS / FIRST CHAPTER</span><h1>A changing empire.<br>A lasting story.</h1><p>Trace the growth and contraction of the ancient Assyrian state against familiar geography. Drag through eleven dated chapters, from the heartland to the empire's final years.</p></div>
<div class="atlas-intro"><p><strong>How to read this map</strong> The shapes are approximate teaching sketches of regions, not exact ancient borders. Patterned areas show a different or less sustained relationship to Assyrian rule. Modern borders are for orientation.</p><a class="text-link" href="#atlas-method">Evidence &amp; method <span aria-hidden="true">&#8595;</span></a></div>
<section class="atlas" aria-label="Interactive historical map" data-atlas >
<div class="atlas-toolbar"><div class="atlas-tabs"><label><input id="map-borders" type="checkbox" checked> Modern borders</label><label><input id="map-labels" type="checkbox" checked> Place names</label><label><input id="map-compare" type="checkbox"> Compare with 671 BCE</label></div><span class="atlas-edition">11 dated sketches / 1350-609 BCE</span></div>
<div class="atlas-timeline"><div class="atlas-timeline-head"><div><span class="eyebrow">MOVE THROUGH TIME</span><label for="map-year">Drag the timeline or choose a chapter</label></div><div class="atlas-playback"><button type="button" id="map-prev" class="icon-button" aria-label="Previous chapter" disabled>&#8592;</button><button type="button" id="map-play" class="button solid" aria-pressed="false" disabled><span aria-hidden="true">&#9654;</span> <span id="map-play-text">Play timeline</span></button><button type="button" id="map-next" class="icon-button" aria-label="Next chapter" disabled>&#8594;</button></div></div>
<input id="map-year" type="range" min="0" max="10" step="1" value="4" aria-valuetext="824 BCE - Looking west under Shalmaneser III" aria-describedby="map-time-note" disabled>
<div class="atlas-ticks" aria-hidden="true"><span>1350 BCE</span><span>859 BCE</span><span>671 BCE</span><span>609 BCE</span></div><div class="atlas-timeline-bottom"><p id="map-time-note">One step = one dated sketch. The intervals contain different numbers of years; boundaries are not interpolated.</p><label for="map-chapter-select" class="sr-only">Choose a historical chapter</label><select id="map-chapter-select" disabled>{options}</select></div></div>
<div class="atlas-grid"><div class="atlas-map-column"><div class="atlas-canvas">
<svg id="historical-map" viewBox="0 0 1000 820" role="img" aria-labelledby="map-svg-title map-svg-description" tabindex="0"><title id="map-svg-title">Assyria at 824 BCE</title><desc id="map-svg-description">An approximate regional map. The selected chapter's text explains the evidence and limitations.</desc><defs><pattern id="atlas-hatch" width="9" height="9" patternUnits="userSpaceOnUse" patternTransform="rotate(35)"><rect width="9" height="9" fill="#c8a668" fill-opacity=".16"/><line x1="0" y1="0" x2="0" y2="9" stroke="#aa7836" stroke-width="2"/></pattern><clipPath id="atlas-frame"><rect width="1000" height="820"/></clipPath><clipPath id="atlas-land-mask"><path id="atlas-land-clip"/></clipPath></defs><g clip-path="url(#atlas-frame)"><rect class="map-sea" width="1000" height="820"/><g id="map-graticule"></g><path id="map-land" class="map-land"/><g id="map-modern-borders"></g><g clip-path="url(#atlas-land-mask)"><g id="map-comparison"></g><g id="map-influence"></g><g id="map-territory"></g></g><g id="map-rivers"></g><g id="map-modern-labels"></g><g id="map-water-labels"></g><g id="map-places"></g></g></svg>
<div class="atlas-map-label"><span class="eyebrow">APPROXIMATE REGIONAL EXTENT</span><strong id="map-date">824 <small>BCE</small></strong></div>
<div class="atlas-zoom" role="group" aria-label="Map zoom controls"><button type="button" id="map-zoom-in" aria-label="Zoom in" disabled>+</button><button type="button" id="map-zoom-out" aria-label="Zoom out" disabled>-</button><button type="button" id="map-reset" aria-label="Reset map view" disabled>&#8634;</button></div>
<p class="atlas-loading" id="map-load-status" role="status">Loading the locally preserved map data...</p>
<p class="atlas-map-help">Zoom with + / - &middot; Drag to pan &middot; Arrow keys move the map</p>
</div><div class="atlas-legend" aria-label="Map legend"><span><i class="legend-control"></i> Broad territorial control</span><span><i class="legend-influence"></i> Indirect, contested or brief control</span><span><i class="legend-city"></i> Historical city</span><span class="legend-comparison" hidden><i></i> 671 BCE comparison</span></div>
<p id="map-place-detail" class="atlas-place-detail">City markers identify places, not the full extent of Assyrian settlement. Select a city in the list for context.</p><label class="atlas-place-picker">Find a historical city<select id="map-place-select" disabled><option value="">Choose a city</option>{''.join(f'<option value="{h(p["id"])}">{h(p["name"])}</option>' for p in data['places'])}</select></label></div>
<aside class="atlas-story" aria-label="Selected historical chapter"><span class="eyebrow" id="map-period">EXPANSION AND TRIBUTE</span><span class="atlas-step" id="map-step">CHAPTER 05 / 11</span><h2 id="map-chapter">Looking west under Shalmaneser III</h2><p id="map-summary">{h(snapshots[4]['summary'])}</p><div class="atlas-caution"><span class="eyebrow">READ WITH CARE</span><p id="map-caution">{h(snapshots[4]['caution'])}</p></div><div class="atlas-story-sources"><span class="eyebrow">EVIDENCE FOR THIS CHAPTER</span><ul id="map-sources"><li><a href="#atlas-sources">See the source notes below</a></li></ul><div id="map-biblical" hidden></div></div><a class="text-link" href="/articles/ancient-assyria/">Read the wider history <span aria-hidden="true">&#8594;</span></a></aside></div>
<div class="atlas-presets" role="group" aria-label="Jump to a chapter"><button data-map-stage="0" disabled>Heartland <span>1350 BCE</span></button><button data-map-stage="4" disabled>Westward <span>824 BCE</span></button><button data-map-stage="7" disabled>Into Egypt <span>671 BCE</span></button><button data-map-stage="10" disabled>Imperial collapse <span>609 BCE</span></button></div>
<noscript><p class="article-note">JavaScript enables the draggable map. You can still read every chapter and download all of the map data below.</p></noscript></section>
<div class="atlas-continuity"><span class="eyebrow">BEYOND THE BORDERS</span><h2>An empire ends. A people's story continues.</h2><p>This first map follows an ancient state. Its territory is not a map of modern Assyrian identity, present-day land claims or every place Assyrians have lived. Explore the archive's later histories, languages and living communities.</p><a class="text-link" href="/timeline/">Continue through the ages &#8594;</a> <a class="text-link" href="/bible/">Read the biblical accounts &#8594;</a></div>
<section id="atlas-method" class="atlas-method"><div><span class="eyebrow">EVIDENCE, OPEN DATA &amp; PRESERVATION</span><h2>Know what the map can tell you.</h2><p>These original, hand-drawn coordinate sketches interpret the regional histories cited below. They have not been digitised from an authoritative historical atlas, and have not received specialist cartographic review. Lines are deliberately generalised; they cannot locate a village inside or outside a historical province.</p><p>The solid layer sketches broad territorial control. Patterning separates tributary relationships, contested regions and short-lived conquests, as explained for each date. These categories also varied within the shaded regions. At 612 and 609 BCE, uncertain surviving boundaries are left unmapped. The city markers provide context instead.</p><p>Present-day coastlines and borders use Natural Earth at 1:110 million scale; the selected rivers use its 1:50 million data. They are an orientation aid: ancient rivers and shorelines could differ. Natural Earth's boundary conventions do not resolve present-day disputes. Label positions are editorial. The map uses a simple regional equirectangular projection.</p><p>There are no external tile services, map accounts or API keys. The JavaScript, geographical files, dated sketches and source notes are served by this repository. Download them, keep the attribution and improve the evidence.</p></div><div class="atlas-downloads"><h3>Keep a copy.</h3><a href="/archive/maps/assyria-atlas.json" download>Historical sketches &amp; source notes <span>JSON / CC BY 4.0</span></a><a href="/archive/maps/natural-earth-land.geojson" download>Land &amp; coastlines <span>GeoJSON / public domain</span></a><a href="/archive/maps/natural-earth-countries.geojson" download>Modern countries <span>GeoJSON / public domain</span></a><a href="/archive/maps/natural-earth-rivers.geojson" download>Rivers <span>GeoJSON / public domain</span></a><a href="/archive/maps/README.md" download>Attribution &amp; methodology <span>Preservation notes</span></a><p>Made with <a href="https://www.naturalearthdata.com/about/terms-of-use/">Natural Earth</a>. Tom Patterson, Nathaniel Vaughn Kelso and contributors. Original atlas text and historical sketches: Assyria | The Living Archive, <a href="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/">CC BY 4.0</a>. Cited scholarship retains its own rights.</p></div></section>
<details class="atlas-text-chapters"><summary>Read all eleven chapters as text</summary><ol>{chronology}</ol></details><section id="atlas-sources" class="atlas-source-notes"><span class="eyebrow">FOLLOW THE EVIDENCE</span><h2>Sources and interpretation.</h2><p>These sources support the chronology and regional narrative. The boundary sketches are this project's interpretation, not geospatial datasets supplied or endorsed by their authors.</p><ol>{sources}</ol></section>
</main>'''
